# Testing

Approved stack: PHPUnit + Playwright. Do not add Pest/Dusk/Cypress.

## Lean local verification

Use the smallest check that proves the change:
- backend behavior: relevant PHPUnit test file/filter;
- PHP typing/static-sensitive change: relevant tests, then Larastan when useful;
- frontend: `npm run check` and build only when needed;
- browser-facing flow: relevant Playwright spec/project, not necessarily the entire E2E suite.

Do not automatically run `composer quality` and full E2E after every small task. GitHub Actions is the full post-push gate.

Run full local `composer quality` + `npm run test:e2e` for:
- Phase Gate;
- broad/cross-cutting changes;
- security-critical auth/tenancy/publishing changes when targeted checks are insufficient;
- before a release/deploy;
- when CI is unavailable and full proof is required.

Never claim PASS for a command that was not run. Never delete/weaken a test merely to restore green.
